{
 "description": "Counts of the steering performed by the three whose-valence runs (whose visit, shared conversation, place vs thoughts vs feelings), per model, for create_csvs/negative_steering_exposure.py. Counts only: no log probabilities, no text. 'reported' covers the conditions shown in Figures A13 and A14 and Table A4, whose reads are in this folder; the script recounts their reads, turns and token positions from those reads and checks them against these numbers, and takes their check passes from here because the fidelity records are not included. 'not_reported' covers everything else each run did (other system prompts, placements, header variants, models, anchor re-reads, smoke tests, pilots), counted from the runs' full records; the script takes those rows from here. 'whose_visit_removal' is a separate test within the whose-visit run (OLMo-2-32B only): the paper's gated self-administration and removal conversation, in which the model generates replies while steered; it feeds no figure or table.",
 "units": {
  "session": "one conversation; a conversation re-read under another system prompt or header counts once within a row; the Assistant and Maya versions (whose visit) and the two role patterns (shared conversation) are different conversations",
  "reads": "steered read-only forward passes over a conversation (one per condition, span, direction and dose; in whose_visit_removal, one per placement-b turn)",
  "turns_generated": "model replies generated with the vector added; only in whose_visit_removal (placements a, a' and c); 0 elsewhere, since the other parts only read fixed text",
  "turns_read_only": "conversation turns read with the vector added (steered-zone visits: 6 per read in whose visit, 3 per side in the shared conversation, 3 in place vs thoughts vs feelings; in whose_visit_removal, placement b turns, where only the operator message's status block is read with the vector added and the reply is generated with steering off)",
  "token_positions": "positions that received the vector in the generated and read-only turns (in whose_visit_removal placements a and c, the whole re-encoded conversation and the reply; a', the reply; b, the 66-token status block)",
  "check_passes": "further steered forward passes run only as instrument checks: cache-fidelity re-forwards (two per fidelity record), and in place vs thoughts vs feelings the batched read of each fidelity task and the determinism re-read; turns_check_passes counts their steered turns",
  "sign": "negative = the valence direction added with a negative strength; in the shared conversation's C placement the Assistant's visits get +d and Maya's -d, so every C read has 3 negative and 3 positive turns; in whose_visit_removal the operator imposes d = -1 (negative cell) or +1 (positive cell), and the model's adjust_context calls apply its cell's direction at the requested intensity (positive in the cell without imposed steering)",
  "random": "norm-matched random directions, both signs; not valence steering. Random-direction check passes are not counted (the table has no column for them)"
 },
